.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Gibbs showed that at fixed temperature and pressure a system reaches equilibrium at the minimum of its total Gibbs energy G = \sum_i n_i\mu_i. For N_2O_4 \rightleftharpoons 2NO_2 this example plots G(\xi) from gibbs_energy_of_mixture at several temperatures and marks the composition returned by solve_equilibrium_composition, which sits at each minimum. The slope dG/d\xi = \sum_i\nu_i\mu_i (the reaction Gibbs energy) crosses zero there.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/thermo/equilibrium/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_02_gibbs_energy_minimization_thumb.png
